Switch's local Python integration and documentation were authored for this project.
It does not include Apple's proprietary OS images in its tracked source.

The optional HakiOS checkout is fetched from:
https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel
Its kernel changes, drivers, loader, binaries and other components retain their
upstream licenses. See that repository's LICENSE/NOTICE, COMPLIANCE.md and
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. Switch verifies the upstream binary hashes; it does
not claim that those binaries were rebuilt locally.

UniXNU and its QEMU device port are separate upstream projects:
https://github.com/UniXNU/UniXNU
https://github.com/xVanTuring/UniXNU-qemu
Their code and any user-built/exported components retain their original licenses.
Apple iOS/iPadOS system files must be supplied separately by the builder.

This project is independent of Apple, Nintendo, HakiOS, UniXNU and Switchroot.
